  message: "DONE in PR #2036 (dev ceca2f496c; lab /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gabak_11032026/RESULT.md, pre-registered in PREREGISTER.md). Both fix candidates shipped in py.py: (1) the chain arm reads a from-imported OBJECT root's import-anchored path (_from_import_receiver_path) beside module_imports, so request.args.get lands as python:flask.request.args:0-0:get:unresolved with an ExternalRef, the same slot the import-flask spelling gets; (2) _emit_module_attr_refs emits module_attr_ref on flask.request for a bare read (request.data). A binding that is a symbol in the tree is refused (no workspace-prefixed phantom, INV-nuzas); the scope-narrowed maps keep a parameter named request on the placeholder (INV-dulum). Also: _dotted_module_of_call takes the from-import binding (from pkg import sub; sub.deep.fn() binds in the tree), and the WI-huhum retarget takes a CLASS read as a value (fields.String -> references), which the A/B showed was needed: 11 in-tree phantoms otherwise. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE: the item's own acceptance, run as production-path tests (test_py_from_import_chain_slot.py): the fixture's edge dst starts with python:flask.request.args:0-0:get:, and verify-claims with a user net_recv row flask.request.args/get (--no-default-overlays) turns untrusted-input-no-host-fs VIOLATED through get -> open (the 2026-11-03 premise check measured 0 flows with that very row); a row flask.request/attributes data does the same through the bare read; without a row the WI-fuzik disclosure still names save. Corpus: flask-restful A/B 10 calls edges external -> qualified (all 10 sampled read correctly), 0 gone, 0 already-qualified changed, +92 external module_attr_ref, +12 references, 0 in-tree slots. mlflow A/B (291k edges): 395 calls edges external -> qualified, every slot external (unittest.mock.patch 297, pyspark.sql.SparkSession.builder 37, flask.request.args 17, ...), 0 resolved edges lost, 0 already-qualified changed, 6 placeholder calls became references to the in-tree constant they read (WI-lovun through the from-import binding), +1083 external module_attr_ref, +742 references, 25 module_attr_ref -> references conversions. Red first: 4 failed / 2 controls passed on the base tree; four mutations each red exactly the predicted set (the in-tree guard answering no reds the six in-tree tests). The first mlflow A/B REFUTED the symbol-lookup guard (27 resolved clint calls lost to the method-call-recovery linker, in-tree slots under re-exports / generated _pb2 names / from-imported submodules); the guard became SymbolResolver.module_in_tree (top-level package, root-anchored) + the suffix-aware lookup, and the second mlflow A/B is in RESULT.md."  # 1d01
